cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this MA2A release candidate, please cite the archived v0.2.0-rc1 software release."
title: "MA2A: Memoria.ia Agent-to-Agent Protocol — v0.2.0-rc1"
type: software
version: "0.2.0-rc1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22866124"
date-released: 2026-09-20
authors:
  - family-names: "Matos"
    given-names: "Marcelo Roldão"
abstract: >-
  MA2A is an experimental protocol and reference implementation for deterministic
  state synchronization and authenticated resilient execution among autonomous
  agents, edge devices and organizational nodes. The v0.2 release-candidate line
  adds a C++20 execution path, Ed25519-signed job/failure evidence, bounded TCP
  transport, deterministic failover through resolutive-routing, adversarial
  validation and reproducible stress gates.
repository-code: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/ma2a"
keywords:
  - "agent-to-agent"
  - "resilient execution"
  - "deterministic routing"
  - "resolutive memory"
  - "edge AI"
  - "Ed25519"
  - "multi-agent systems"
